<Layout title="About the research catalog | Reverse Engineer Lab"><article class="detail narrow"><div class="eyebrow">ABOUT THE INDEX</div><h1>Understanding,<br/><em>with receipts.</em></h1><p class="lede">Reverse Engineer Lab is an independent catalog of reverse engineering research and case studies. It is not affiliated with Reverse Engineer Anything.</p><section class="article-section"><h2>Research takes different shapes</h2><p>A binary analysis, API investigation, or architecture teardown will not produce the same report. The shared foundation is a clear question, a target and revision, findings, public evidence, and honest limitations.</p></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Separate observation from inference</h2><p>Observed facts come from inspected artifacts or measured behavior. Inferences explain what those facts might mean. Unknowns describe where the evidence ends. Publication means an editor reviewed the submission, not that every conclusion is independently reproduced.</p></section><section class="article-section"><h2>Contribute safely</h2><p>Share original text and public HTTPS links. Prefer evidence pinned to a revision. Do not submit credentials, private links, personal data, or proprietary source. We do not fetch or execute submitted URLs. Editors can approve a submission or deny it with a recorded reason.</p><a class="text-link" href="/submit">Submit an investigation ↗</a></section></article></Layout>
